# ---------------------------------------------------------------- corpora
# 8 GB of third-party sign-language data. Never commit it: INCLUDE alone is
# 56.8 GB of source video, the licences are the upstream projects' to grant,
# and every fetch script here reproduces it exactly.
#
#   data/fetch_video.sh   INCLUDE raw video (Zenodo 4010759, CC BY 4.0)
#   data/fetch_poses_all.sh
#   data/fetch_cislr.sh   CISLR (gated, AFL-3.0)
# `data/*` and not `data/`: git never descends into an excluded DIRECTORY, so
# the negations below can never fire under `data/`. The existing fetch scripts
# only survived because gitignore does not apply to already-tracked files --
# data/fetch_islgov.sh was silently unstageable until this was fixed.
data/*
!data/*.sh
!data/README*

# --------------------------------------------------------------- environments
.venv/
.venv-tf/
.venv-mp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/

# --------------------------------------------------------------- build output
app/dist/
app/.vite/
.DS_Store

# ------------------------------------------------------------- pipeline state
# Locks, PIDs and logs for the long-running fetch/extract jobs. Machine-local
# by definition — and the reason these live in the repo rather than /tmp is
# that macOS wiping /tmp killed the pipeline twice.
run/

# ---------------------------------------------------------- large checkpoints
# The Keras checkpoints are 6-11 MB each and regenerable from train/train.py.
# The TF.js model in app/public/model/ IS committed: it is 2.1 MB and the app
# cannot run without it, which matters more than repo size for a demo people
# are meant to be able to clone and try.
models/*.keras
models/*.h5
models/saved_model/
models/holistic_landmarker.task

# Own recordings may contain identifiable video of real people. Contributors
# should share these deliberately, not by accident.
setu-recordings-*.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------ editor/agent
# Local tooling config — machine-specific, not part of the project.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# --------------------------------------------------------------------- secrets
.env
.env.*
*.pem

# Stitch design export: the unpacked directory is kept as reference, the zip
# was an exact duplicate of it.
stitch_setu_healthcare_communication_bridge.zip
